WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.380
Everyone knows what a Jedi is — but who's
in charge of the Jedi Order?

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:07.020
And what happens to trainees who don't pass
their tests?

00:00:07.150 --> 00:00:10.860
If you're wondering about the hierarchy of
the galaxy's guardians of justice and peace,

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:11.640
here's your guide.

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:16.820
The lowest rank in the Jedi hierarchy are
Jedi Younglings, also known as initiates.

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:21.539
According to the book Jedi vs. Sith: The Essential
Guide to the Force, younglings are children

00:00:21.539 --> 00:00:25.490
sensitive to the Force who were gathered from
across the galaxy as infants to be trained

00:00:25.490 --> 00:00:26.400
as future Jedi.

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:31.359
The Jedi Path: A Manual for Students of the
Force explains that at one time, young adults

00:00:31.359 --> 00:00:36.440
and adolescents were recruited as Jedi Younglings,
but the Order found that these older recruits

00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:40.300
were already exposed to negative emotions
that could push them to the dark side.

00:00:40.780 --> 00:00:45.190
As a result, the Jedi began recruiting children
who were younger, and more innocent.

00:00:45.190 --> 00:00:47.080
Younglings don't train with mentors one-on-one.

00:00:47.240 --> 00:00:51.560
Instead, they're separated into small groups
called clans, and train together within those

00:00:51.560 --> 00:00:52.060
clans.

00:00:52.180 --> 00:00:56.960
Once younglings learn their basics, they must
take a series of tests known as the Initiate

00:00:56.960 --> 00:01:00.540
Trials, which have included such tasks as
building a lightsaber.

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:04.250
Though the Initiate Trials have changed over
time, their ultimate goal is to determine

00:01:04.250 --> 00:01:07.900
students' knowledge of the Jedi Code and ability
to conquer the Dark Side.

00:01:08.420 --> 00:01:12.820
Unlike the group training for younglings,
Padawans receive one-on-one coaching in real-life

00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:15.960
missions — a significant hurdle for most
Padawans to clear.

00:01:18.280 --> 00:01:19.180
"Oh, it's you!"

00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:24.000
Similar to younglings, Padawans must also
pass a series of trials to move up in rank.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:28.540
These tests include the Trial of Skill, the
Trial of Courage, the Trial of Flesh, the

00:01:28.540 --> 00:01:31.140
Trial of Spirit, and the Trial of Insight.

00:01:31.450 --> 00:01:35.880
The Trials test a Padawan's mental and physical
abilities and determine if they are ready

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:37.600
to become a full-fledged Jedi.

00:01:37.720 --> 00:01:40.000
"The Force is with you, young Skywalker.

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:44.160
But you are not a Jedi yet."

00:01:44.380 --> 00:01:47.320
Not every Padawan graduates to the rank of
Jedi Knight.

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:51.360
But unsuccessful initiates can still become
members of the Jedi Service Corps.

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:57.240
This organization is separated into four arms:
Agricultural, Medical, Educational, and Exploration.

00:01:57.380 --> 00:02:01.420
The Agricultural Corps use the Force to help
ensure that the Republic has enough food to

00:02:01.420 --> 00:02:01.980
go around.

00:02:02.420 --> 00:02:06.210
The Medical Corps is considered one of the
most advanced medical organizations in the

00:02:06.210 --> 00:02:10.950
Republic, with its members performing specialized
procedures and triage work on battlefields

00:02:10.950 --> 00:02:11.980
across the galaxy.

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:16.740
The Educational Corps work with the Jedi archives,
translating and updating records.

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:21.940
The most exciting branch is arguably the Exploration
Corps, whose members are sent to the far-flung

00:02:21.940 --> 00:02:24.000
corners of space to make new discoveries.

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:28.860
Jedi Knights are fully-fledged members of
the Order, expected to uphold peace in the

00:02:28.860 --> 00:02:30.760
galaxy and the ideals of the Jedi Code.

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:35.560
The most common way to become a Jedi Knight
is by passing trials as a Padawan, but an

00:02:35.560 --> 00:02:40.340
individual can also be granted the title by
performing a heroic deed, like Obi-Wan Kenobi

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:42.520
assuming the rank after defeating Darth Maul.

00:02:42.520 --> 00:02:46.880
At this point in the hierarchy, Jedi Knights
still have much to learn about the Force,

00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:51.340
but they no longer carry out their duties
under the direct supervision of a Jedi Master.

00:02:51.460 --> 00:02:55.460
Most Jedi Knights carry out their missions
alone, testing their self-discipline and upholding

00:02:55.460 --> 00:02:57.040
the principles of the Jedi Code.

00:02:57.740 --> 00:03:01.940
When people think of the Jedi, two things
usually come to mind: the Force and lightsabers.

00:03:02.120 --> 00:03:03.020
"Who are the Jedi?"

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:07.160
In many cases, those who specialize in the
manipulation of the Force pursue the title

00:03:07.160 --> 00:03:08.400
of Jedi Consular.

00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:13.060
Most of these Jedi are focused on using their
connection to the Force to resolve conflicts

00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:13.960
in a peaceful way.

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:19.640
The most esteemed Jedi Consular Masters serve
on the Reconciliation Council, a select group

00:03:19.640 --> 00:03:23.980
of Jedi who work directly with the Republic
Diplomatic Corps to engage in diplomacy and

00:03:23.980 --> 00:03:25.620
interplanetary relations.

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:29.920
There are many different ways for Jedi Consulars
to use their talents within the Order.

00:03:30.190 --> 00:03:34.820
Jedi Seers use deep meditation to connect
to the Force and receive visions of the past,

00:03:34.820 --> 00:03:35.680
present, and future.

00:03:35.950 --> 00:03:39.780
For instance, the prophecy of the one who
will bring balance to the Force was the product

00:03:39.790 --> 00:03:44.710
of visions received by Jedi Seers who recorded
their findings in the Jedi Archives.

00:03:44.710 --> 00:03:48.840
Other Consulars become Jedi Healers, who use
their connection to the Force to mend broken

00:03:48.840 --> 00:03:49.340
bodies.

00:03:49.460 --> 00:03:54.740
Others work as Jedi Ambassadors and Jedi Diplomats,
serving as representatives in various government

00:03:54.740 --> 00:03:56.900
bodies and activist movements respectively.

00:03:56.900 --> 00:04:02.080
Other Consulars might become Jedi Lorekeepers,
dedicated to maintaining to the Jedi Archives.

00:04:02.860 --> 00:04:06.260
In the years leading up to the Clone Wars,
the Republic had no standing army.

00:04:06.580 --> 00:04:10.920
Instead, specialized Jedi Knights known as
Guardians acted as the first line of defense

00:04:10.920 --> 00:04:11.720
for the galaxy.

00:04:11.880 --> 00:04:17.540
Guardians are divided into three main subclasses:
Peacekeepers, Temple Security, and Starfighters.

00:04:17.540 --> 00:04:22.460
Peacekeepers act as galactic police, trained
in crowd control and deescalation of threats.

00:04:22.820 --> 00:04:26.600
Jedi assigned to Temple Security protect the
Jedi Temple on the planet Coruscant.

00:04:26.600 --> 00:04:30.620
As their name implies, Starfighters serve
as the pilots of the Jedi Order.

00:04:30.620 --> 00:04:35.100
Particularly gifted Jedi Guardians may be
known as Battlemasters, tasked with teaching

00:04:35.100 --> 00:04:38.600
lightsaber form and techniques, or cadences,
to Jedi in training.

00:04:38.970 --> 00:04:42.720
Some Guardians come to specialize in fighting
with weapons other than a lightsaber, being

00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:45.420
awarded the title of Exotic Weapons Specialist.

00:04:45.560 --> 00:04:50.540
These weapons can include whips, flails, blasters,
and even double-bladed lightsabers.

00:04:50.960 --> 00:04:53.440
Jedi Sentinels are like the Order's wild cards.

00:04:53.440 --> 00:04:57.640
Sentinels pursue training in disciplines that
are also available to non-force sensitive

00:04:57.640 --> 00:04:58.140
beings.

00:04:58.260 --> 00:05:02.880
In doing so, they add modern insight and skills
to the the Jedi Order's ancient teachings.

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:07.440
Common pursuits for Jedi Sentinels include
specializing in computer systems, manipulation

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:11.140
of technology, and hacking into and disabling
security mechanisms.

00:05:11.300 --> 00:05:15.780
Other Sentinels do exceedingly well on missions
that require stealth and infiltration.

00:05:15.780 --> 00:05:20.430
One particular group of Sentinels known as
the Jedi Shadows serve as the Order's assassins

00:05:20.430 --> 00:05:23.550
and excel at sneaky, less combat-oriented
tasks.

00:05:23.550 --> 00:05:27.930
Jedi Sentinels are also distinguished by often
remaining in one area for much longer than

00:05:27.930 --> 00:05:31.760
other Jedi, acting as Watchmen for particular
regions of the galaxy.

00:05:32.440 --> 00:05:36.919
If a Jedi has shown exemplary skill, deep
knowledge of the Force, and successfully trained

00:05:36.920 --> 00:05:41.120
an apprentice to become a Jedi Knight, they
may be granted the title of Jedi Master.

00:05:43.180 --> 00:05:45.780
"Don't f--- with a Jedi Master, son."

00:05:46.060 --> 00:05:50.120
A Master's purpose is to be a positive force
in the galaxy, and to expand the influence

00:05:50.120 --> 00:05:50.960
of the Jedi Order.

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:55.120
What separates a Jedi Master from a Jedi Knight
is that their exceptional achievements and

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:59.020
experience make them uniquely qualified to
teach the younger members of the Order.

00:05:59.380 --> 00:06:03.320
In addition to teaching younger Jedi, they
are also naturally fit to lead the Order,

00:06:03.320 --> 00:06:07.260
not just by example, but by sitting on one
of the four Jedi Councils that govern the

00:06:07.260 --> 00:06:07.760
Order.

00:06:08.140 --> 00:06:12.760
The four councils are known as the Council
of First Knowledge, the Council of Reconciliation,

00:06:12.760 --> 00:06:14.780
the Council of Reassignment, and the High
Council.

00:06:14.980 --> 00:06:19.010
The Council of First Knowledge oversees the
education of younger Jedi and the dissemination

00:06:19.010 --> 00:06:21.020
of materials from the Jedi Archives.

00:06:21.160 --> 00:06:24.820
This council is usually comprised of Consulars
who became Lorekeepers.

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:28.720
The Council of Reconciliation, meanwhile,
deals in politics and diplomacy.

00:06:28.820 --> 00:06:33.980
This council is also regularly filled with
Consulars, as well as Diplomats and Ambassadors.

00:06:34.320 --> 00:06:39.020
The Council of Reassignment governs the Jedi
Service Corps, dictating which body each initiate

00:06:39.020 --> 00:06:42.880
will be funneled into after they fail to advance
on the path to Jedi Knighthood.

00:06:42.880 --> 00:06:45.220
These councils are all governed by the High
Council.

00:06:45.460 --> 00:06:49.740
During the Clone Wars, the High Council was
made up of five lifetime appointees, four

00:06:49.740 --> 00:06:54.400
long-term appointees, and three short-term
appointees, making for a total of 12 council

00:06:54.400 --> 00:06:54.900
members.

00:06:54.940 --> 00:06:58.940
The High Council oversees everything within
the Order and is crucial to its stability

00:06:58.940 --> 00:06:59.660
and success.

00:07:00.140 --> 00:07:03.940
The highest ranking member within the High
Council is given the title Master of the Order.

00:07:04.160 --> 00:07:08.040
This prestigious position is only obtained
by those who have demonstrated incredible

00:07:08.040 --> 00:07:09.440
knowledge of the ways of the Jedi.

00:07:09.930 --> 00:07:13.580
In the years leading up to the Clone Wars,
the title of Master of the Order was held

00:07:13.580 --> 00:07:15.540
by Lifetime Appointee Mace Windu.

00:07:15.720 --> 00:07:20.380
After the Clone Wars began, Master Windu decided
to take a more active role in commanding troops

00:07:20.380 --> 00:07:24.020
on the battlefield, and insisted that the
title be passed to Master Yoda.

00:07:24.240 --> 00:07:28.340
Though Master of the Order is a prestigious
position, they are still outranked by one

00:07:28.340 --> 00:07:30.500
final position: the Grand Master.

00:07:31.220 --> 00:07:35.720
The Grand Master is the most prestigious rank
in the Jedi hierarchy, awarded to only the

00:07:35.720 --> 00:07:37.520
wisest and most skilled.

00:07:37.720 --> 00:07:41.420
The Jedi High Council must unanimously vote
to bestow the title onto them.

00:07:41.660 --> 00:07:46.040
Grand Masters often serve in conjunction with
the Master of the Order, leading the Jedi

00:07:46.040 --> 00:07:46.620
High Council.

00:07:46.720 --> 00:07:50.860
While at one time several Jedi Masters could
be given the title at once, that practice

00:07:50.860 --> 00:07:53.020
ended long before the time of the Clone Wars.

00:07:53.240 --> 00:07:56.820
One of the most critical roles held by the
Grand Master is to pass on their knowledge

00:07:56.820 --> 00:07:58.660
to the next generation of Jedi.

00:07:58.800 --> 00:08:02.120
Part of this duty involves training younglings
in the ways of the Force.

00:08:02.200 --> 00:08:04.940
Two notable figures have achieved the title
of Grand Master.

00:08:05.190 --> 00:08:09.580
During the Clone Wars, Master Yoda was recognized
as the Grand Master of the Jedi Order.

00:08:09.590 --> 00:08:14.050
Afterward, at least in the old Expanded Universe
books, Luke Skywalker invokes the title of

00:08:14.050 --> 00:08:18.160
Grand Master as he rebuilds the Jedi Order
following the fall of the Empire.

